# Frontend patterns

Use this only when the React profile is active. Full reference: .ai/skills/frontend-patterns.

- Components use props.x, not destructuring.
- useEffect belongs in components, not custom hooks.
- Custom hooks use one grouped useState and expose domain operations.
- Context is dependency injection only, not shared state.
- Store hooks hide React Query internals behind domain helpers.
- CSS Modules only; no utility CSS frameworks.
